WEBVTT

00:02.302 --> 00:03.769
Legend has it that...

00:04.938 --> 00:07.736
...during the Heian Period, there were
men who fought with no weapons...

00:08.074 --> 00:13.410
They were known as the Men of
Carnage and they reigned undefeated.

00:14.881 --> 00:20.046
Their technique was called
the Mutsu Enmei Style.

00:33.166 --> 00:40.595
<i>The Age of Chaos</i>
<i>Mutsu Enmei Style Gaiden</i>

00:40.874 --> 00:46.710
<i>Rushing through my innocent</i>
<i>youth without a care in the world.</i>

00:48.248 --> 00:54.153
<i>This soul of mine is</i>
<i>so easy to influence.</i>

00:55.822 --> 00:59.588
<i>WORRY ABOUT IDENTITY</i>

00:59.693 --> 01:02.890
<i>WORRY ABOUT IDENTITY</i>

01:06.666 --> 01:13.731
<i>This is what I'm wishing</i>
<i>for as I sing this song.</i>

01:13.907 --> 01:19.743
<i>I want you to acknowledge</i>
<i>me, that's all.</i>

01:20.614 --> 01:27.884
<i>You smiled at me for</i>
<i>the very first time.</i>

01:28.054 --> 01:36.462
<i>Thank you so much, thank you</i>
<i>from the bottom of my heart.</i>

01:37.163 --> 01:38.824
<i>I'll never forget it.</i>

01:48.575 --> 01:52.011
<i>The Age of Chaos</i>
<i>Mutsu Enmei Style Gaiden</i>

02:02.622 --> 02:04.749
But you weren't going for the kill.

02:05.058 --> 02:07.891
I know that wasn't anywhere
near your best stuff...

02:08.495 --> 02:11.487
Oh, you don't think so?

02:11.631 --> 02:14.759
I'd like to make you go for the kill...

02:16.469 --> 02:20.496
<i>Patriot of the Sea</i>

02:29.549 --> 02:31.414
Lord Sakamoto, please stop him!

02:31.618 --> 02:34.951
If Izumi keeps talking like that,
it will escalate into a fight!

02:35.188 --> 02:36.712
Of course it will.

02:36.956 --> 02:39.424
Izumi's picking a fight
with that kid, after all.

02:39.659 --> 02:40.751
But why?

02:42.262 --> 02:44.196
Probably so he can show me...

02:49.669 --> 02:51.864
Go on, draw, kid!

02:57.711 --> 02:58.939
You draw, too.

02:59.546 --> 03:03.141
My style is to fight barehanded,
I'll take you on like this.

03:03.650 --> 03:06.118
So he's a grappler, is he?

03:07.020 --> 03:11.081
But that ki, that's no
ordinary boy we're looking at.

03:11.891 --> 03:15.054
Can you win barehanded, Izumi?

03:20.200 --> 03:21.497
Lord Sakamoto...

03:21.634 --> 03:23.295
Nothing to worry about.

03:23.436 --> 03:25.131
Nobody's going to get hurt.

03:25.271 --> 03:26.670
But...

03:27.474 --> 03:30.705
...that Okita boy, he's dead serious.

03:33.046 --> 03:34.638
And he's powerful, too.

03:35.882 --> 03:39.841
Lord Sakamoto, how can
you stand there so calmly?

03:43.156 --> 03:47.525
It must be just as clear to you, he's not
using an ordinary swordsman's stance.

03:48.128 --> 03:50.926
You shouldn't overestimate
Izumi's abilities...

03:51.030 --> 03:53.123
...or else Izumi could
end up in serious danger...

03:53.399 --> 03:56.562
No, he could even get himself killed!

03:58.171 --> 03:59.695
That's a nice evil glare.

04:20.860 --> 04:23.055
Did he miss on purpose just now?

04:23.296 --> 04:25.491
If that boy decides
to slash him for real...

04:30.036 --> 04:31.401
Interesting...

05:04.737 --> 05:07.535
What kind of thrust was
that? I didn't even see it...

05:07.941 --> 05:10.842
That was the Two-Step Thrust.

05:11.010 --> 05:12.534
But, never mind that...

05:15.014 --> 05:16.743
This time, I'm not going to miss!

05:17.584 --> 05:19.950
He missed on purpose
that time as well?

05:21.221 --> 05:23.553
That's enough, Soushi.
You'd better stop now.

05:26.559 --> 05:27.856
Hijikata...

05:28.194 --> 05:30.162
Put away your sword, Soushi.

05:30.730 --> 05:31.856
Uh, all right.

05:34.868 --> 05:36.961
I'm sure you've gotten what you
wanted...

05:37.170 --> 05:38.296
Now go.

05:38.605 --> 05:41.472
This Shieikan Dojo is
full of surprises, huh?

05:41.574 --> 05:44.270
One awesome fighter
after another is appearing!

05:46.613 --> 05:48.046
Let's go then, okay, Ryoma?

05:48.181 --> 05:49.079
Uh-huh.

05:49.816 --> 05:50.783
Sorry to bother you.

05:51.184 --> 05:52.981
Why don't you tell us your name?

05:53.286 --> 05:57.188
Mutsu Enmei Style, Izumi Mutsu.

05:57.590 --> 06:00.184
My name's Toshizou Hijikata.

06:00.660 --> 06:03.993
Izumi Mutsu and Ryoma Sakamoto...

06:04.297 --> 06:06.322
I'll make sure I remember
your names and faces.

06:06.466 --> 06:08.696
We lost to you today...

06:08.801 --> 06:13.363
But in the future, if I ever
find you standing in my way...

06:14.374 --> 06:16.842
...then I'll kill you myself!

06:23.249 --> 06:26.582
Hijikata, why did you
tell them that we lost?

06:26.686 --> 06:27.584
I didn't...

06:27.687 --> 06:29.177
Take a look at your scabbard.

06:38.264 --> 06:42.166
When he dodged your first thrust,
he kicked you in the scabbard.

06:43.069 --> 06:45.731
Had he been serious,
you'd be dead now.

06:46.506 --> 06:48.804
Does it make you happy that
he cracked your scabbard?

06:48.908 --> 06:50.432
Yes, it makes me happy!

06:50.843 --> 06:51.810
Really?

06:51.911 --> 06:53.378
Do you think we'll meet again?

06:53.780 --> 06:55.270
Sure we will...

06:55.415 --> 06:57.007
...we'll cross paths again...

06:57.116 --> 06:58.913
I have a definite
feeling that we will...

06:59.385 --> 07:01.216
Next time I see him, I'll win.

07:01.387 --> 07:04.254
Hijikata, that man is mine, okay?

07:04.424 --> 07:05.823
Listen to you!

07:10.363 --> 07:11.664
<i>Chiba Dojo</i>

07:11.664 --> 07:13.366
<i>Chiba Dojo</i>
Sakamoto Sensei?

07:13.366 --> 07:13.566
<i>Chiba Dojo</i>

07:13.566 --> 07:15.090
<i>Chiba Dojo</i>
He's not here at the moment...

07:17.036 --> 07:18.264
Well! Takechi!

07:18.371 --> 07:19.599
And Nakaoka, too.

07:19.839 --> 07:21.602
We were told that Ryoma's out.

07:21.708 --> 07:23.903
That's right, he went out
to see the cherry blossoms.

07:24.043 --> 07:24.975
That guy!

07:25.078 --> 07:29.105
Off looking at flowers, when he hasn't
even stopped by the Tosa residence?

07:29.215 --> 07:30.409
Uh...

07:45.798 --> 07:49.165
Juutaro, I want you to speak
to Ryoma about this, too!

07:49.302 --> 07:51.770
This is an issue of national importance!

07:51.871 --> 07:55.500
The Americans are trying to intimidate
the Bakufu with their Kurofune to...

07:55.641 --> 07:58.075
...make us sign their one-sided treaty!

07:58.978 --> 08:02.573
The Emperor is in despair, fearing
the contamination of our country!

08:02.782 --> 08:05.250
If the Americans choose
to meet us with force...

08:05.351 --> 08:07.751
...then why shouldn't we also use
force to drive out the foreigners?

08:07.887 --> 08:09.286
Expel the Foreigners!

08:09.489 --> 08:12.390
No, if the Bakufu can't
stand up to the foreigners...

08:12.525 --> 08:14.550
...then we'll have to
overthrow the Bakufu!

08:16.262 --> 08:18.423
Calm down, will you, Nakaoka?

08:18.564 --> 08:22.330
It's not Juutaro's fault
that Ryoma's not here.

08:22.802 --> 08:23.996
Takechi...

08:25.705 --> 08:26.933
Nakaoka...

08:27.240 --> 08:30.300
Listen, have you ever seen the
Kurofune?

08:33.646 --> 08:35.170
Father!

08:35.281 --> 08:36.839
Joukichi Sensei!

08:36.983 --> 08:39.747
Shame on you for
mimicking Ryoma like that!

08:40.853 --> 08:42.013
Sorry, sorry!

08:42.622 --> 08:44.112
But Nakaoka...

08:46.526 --> 08:47.322
What is it, sir?

08:47.660 --> 08:51.152
This is the third time you've
graced us with that speech of yours.

08:51.464 --> 08:54.797
And as I recall, that's the answer
Ryoma gave you the other day...

08:54.934 --> 08:56.765
I couldn't resist!

08:57.470 --> 09:01.133
You're right, that's exactly
what Ryoma said the other day...

09:01.941 --> 09:03.101
Nakaoka...

09:03.209 --> 09:05.871
Listen, have you ever seen the
Kurofune?

09:06.712 --> 09:07.906
No, but...

09:08.014 --> 09:10.710
I've seen them. Those ships are
amazing!

09:11.818 --> 09:13.786
They're gigantic, like this!

09:13.986 --> 09:17.683
You can shout "Expel the Foreigners"
all you want, but you'll never sink them!

09:18.057 --> 09:19.251
Ryoma...

09:19.392 --> 09:22.156
Ryoma, are you in favor
of opening up the country?

09:23.396 --> 09:24.761
I don't know.

09:24.931 --> 09:27.422
I don't really understand
those kinds of details.

09:27.567 --> 09:30.365
That's why I'm leaving all that to you.

09:33.673 --> 09:37.268
I see, that was Ryoma's
way of dodging the question...

09:37.810 --> 09:42.645
But Sensei, couldn't you have
a word with Ryoma yourself?

09:43.716 --> 09:44.842
Me, speak to him?

09:45.651 --> 09:48.051
Ryoma is the kind of man who can...

09:48.154 --> 09:50.679
...and will accomplish many
things for this country.

09:50.823 --> 09:53.121
He is a man of uncommon ability...

09:53.359 --> 09:54.656
Certainly...

09:54.760 --> 09:59.197
So how can we allow such a man to
fritter away his time like this?

09:59.699 --> 10:03.658
Juutaro, he didn't happen to go
out with that fellow again, did he?

10:04.003 --> 10:07.666
If by "that fellow" you mean Izumi...

10:07.840 --> 10:10.172
Well, yes, he did accompany Ryoma.

10:10.576 --> 10:12.441
Who the hell is that guy, anyway?

10:12.545 --> 10:16.106
I hear that Ryoma hasn't come
by the Tosa residence once...

10:16.249 --> 10:18.114
...ever since that fellow showed up!

10:18.518 --> 10:22.215
But if he's the one who is able to
awaken Ryoma's slumbering dragon...

10:22.355 --> 10:23.686
What will you do then?

10:24.657 --> 10:26.352
Joukichi Sensei!

10:26.559 --> 10:28.424
What do you mean by "awaken"?

10:29.595 --> 10:32.155
Ryoma's sword is still asleep.

10:32.265 --> 10:36.395
So? It's not his swordsmanship
that we want Ryoma to focus on.

10:38.171 --> 10:40.605
There's a chance, Nakaoka, that...

10:40.740 --> 10:44.642
...Ryoma might have just the kind of
awakening that you're all hoping for!

10:45.011 --> 10:46.603
What exactly do you mean?

10:46.913 --> 10:50.007
Who knows what might come to pass?

10:50.516 --> 10:51.847
Father!

10:52.585 --> 10:56.544
If that man is one of the
legendary Mutsus, that is...

11:06.866 --> 11:10.597
Both Lord Sakamoto and Izumi...

11:10.736 --> 11:13.728
...their recklessness
really defies belief!

11:13.906 --> 11:18.002
Trying to provoke a fight at a dojo
that we just happened to pass by...

11:21.047 --> 11:24.847
Lord Sakamoto said
"So he can show me..."

11:24.984 --> 11:25.848
But why?

11:26.953 --> 11:30.684
To make Lord Sakamoto
finally go for the kill?

12:18.004 --> 12:20.472
The cherry blossoms are gorgeous!

12:20.606 --> 12:21.231
Yeah...

12:23.476 --> 12:25.444
Let's do it, Izumi...

12:30.683 --> 12:32.048
Uh, Lord Sakamoto?

12:32.184 --> 12:33.811
What are you going to do?

12:33.953 --> 12:36.547
Miss Sanako, could
you please stand back?

12:36.689 --> 12:38.088
Lord Sakamoto...

12:39.558 --> 12:43.016
Looks like I've really
been asleep all this time...

12:43.195 --> 12:45.891
Joukichi Sensei told me
that I've been slumbering...

12:46.365 --> 12:50.062
But the thing is, I had thought I
was giving it my all until now.

12:50.269 --> 12:53.705
I thought he was just
overestimating my abilities...

12:53.906 --> 12:57.239
But watching you fight just now...

12:57.343 --> 12:59.334
...ever since then,
I've had the shivers!

12:59.645 --> 13:01.670
This has never happened to me before!

13:01.814 --> 13:04.214
Maybe I was asleep, but I
think I might be awake now!

13:04.550 --> 13:06.780
I was lucky to meet
an opponent like him...

13:06.886 --> 13:09.616
To have mastered that
thrusting technique at his age...

13:09.789 --> 13:12.223
He'll be someone to
reckon with in five years...

13:12.558 --> 13:14.025
What is he talking about?

13:14.126 --> 13:18.256
True, that Okita boy did have
an amazing thrusting technique...

13:18.397 --> 13:21.924
...but is that any reason for
Lord Sakamoto and Izumi to fight?

13:26.539 --> 13:31.169
I've never been so eager
to fight in my life before!

13:32.178 --> 13:33.372
Neither have I...

13:39.752 --> 13:40.980
He drew!

13:41.153 --> 13:46.352
This is the first time I've ever seen Lord
Sakamoto actually draw his sword...

14:05.111 --> 14:08.547
I have never seen Lord Sakamoto
with such a serious look on his face.

14:26.265 --> 14:28.096
Cha, cha, cha!

14:31.003 --> 14:32.334
So powerful!

14:32.471 --> 14:35.634
He actually dodged Lord
Sakamoto's attack and...

14:35.875 --> 14:37.866
...switched to the
offensive, barehanded!

14:39.345 --> 14:41.006
Then that means...

14:41.313 --> 14:44.874
Okita didn't miss with
his thrust on purpose...

14:46.485 --> 14:48.180
He dodged it?

14:59.698 --> 15:01.290
The one-handed jodan?

15:01.467 --> 15:03.526
That's the same
move he used to defeat...

15:03.636 --> 15:06.298
...Lord Katsura in the
Shogun's Tournament...

15:09.208 --> 15:10.903
Lord Sakamoto...

15:20.419 --> 15:21.249
He blocked it!

15:45.444 --> 15:48.311
W-What was that move?

15:49.648 --> 15:51.809
Just as I thought,
you're an amazing fighter.

15:51.951 --> 15:55.512
You didn't just block my Whirlwind
move, you also slashed at my back leg.

15:55.621 --> 15:58.715
Cha, cha, cha! You're
the one who's a handful!

15:59.492 --> 16:04.452
So it's not going to do me any
good to swing my sword around...

16:09.268 --> 16:11.293
He's going for the thrust!

16:33.459 --> 16:36.587
At this distance, no
kick of his can reach me!

16:36.795 --> 16:38.057
So...

16:38.497 --> 16:41.398
Let's see what you can do with
a 2-step thrust to the chest!

17:00.386 --> 17:03.184
Lord Sakamoto has lost the match?

17:04.523 --> 17:05.785
Lord Sakamoto!

17:07.426 --> 17:09.121
Don't worry, I'm alive.

17:14.767 --> 17:18.203
The sky is really high, huh, Izumi?

17:19.204 --> 17:20.501
Yeah...

17:22.174 --> 17:23.801
You beat me...

17:23.909 --> 17:25.069
I lost!

17:25.210 --> 17:27.144
You're unbelievable, you know that?

17:27.713 --> 17:29.374
It was a close match...

17:29.548 --> 17:32.847
I've never felt my heart
pound like this before.

17:32.952 --> 17:37.116
Anyway, you're just too gentle
for your own good, aren't you?

17:37.623 --> 17:40.148
At the last second, you
slowed down that thrust.

17:40.292 --> 17:42.590
Otherwise, I might not
have grabbed your sword...

17:42.828 --> 17:46.229
Cha, cha, cha!
That was the best I could do!

17:46.665 --> 17:51.193
Anyway, you held back with that
kick, so who are you to talk?

17:52.004 --> 17:53.528
Lord Sakamoto?

17:53.639 --> 17:55.129
Miss Sanako...

17:55.240 --> 17:58.266
As of today, I'm putting down my sword.

17:58.711 --> 17:59.803
But why?

18:00.479 --> 18:02.504
I'm not the brightest guy...

18:02.648 --> 18:05.742
...so I thought I'd try to become
the best swordsman in Japan.

18:05.884 --> 18:08.717
But there's always
someone better than you...

18:08.854 --> 18:10.014
Lord Sakamoto...

18:10.723 --> 18:15.524
The thing is, I've always felt
something calling to me, deep inside...

18:15.761 --> 18:18.924
If I managed to beat Izumi today...

18:19.131 --> 18:22.464
...I would have turned my back
on it, and lived by my sword...

18:22.568 --> 18:24.001
...that's what I'd decided...

18:27.473 --> 18:28.872
Izumi...

18:29.141 --> 18:30.870
Tell me, do you have a dream?

18:31.176 --> 18:32.040
Yes.

18:38.717 --> 18:40.184
What is this, anyway?

18:40.486 --> 18:42.954
I've been told, it's the world!

18:43.088 --> 18:44.282
Oh?

18:45.057 --> 18:47.321
Apparently, this is our country.

18:47.493 --> 18:49.484
You mean it's this small?

18:49.728 --> 18:54.631
It's not really small, it's just that
the whole world is incredibly big.

18:56.468 --> 18:59.460
I'll bet there's plenty
of powerful men out there.

18:59.838 --> 19:02.272
I'd like the chance to take them on.

19:02.441 --> 19:04.466
I'll fight them, and find out for myself...

19:04.576 --> 19:07.602
...if there's anything in the world more
powerful than the Mutsu Enmei Style.

19:07.746 --> 19:11.682
That's my dream, no, it's the
Mutsu clan's dream, I guess.

19:11.817 --> 19:14.513
Cha, cha, cha! Take on the world?

19:14.720 --> 19:18.417
Now that's really something
to blow your own trumpet about!

19:18.557 --> 19:21.082
But I think you're going to do it!

19:21.226 --> 19:22.784
What's your dream, Ryoma?

19:23.529 --> 19:24.962
Me?

19:33.706 --> 19:35.867
I'd like to have a Kurofune of my own...

19:36.241 --> 19:37.469
So it was the Kurofune...

19:37.643 --> 19:42.273
...that's been calling to you deep
inside your heart, Lord Sakamoto?

19:42.648 --> 19:43.842
That's right.

19:44.116 --> 19:45.606
Think that's funny?

19:46.518 --> 19:49.316
All that political talk
is way over my head...

19:49.421 --> 19:52.151
...but I do understand
about the Kurofune...

19:52.991 --> 19:58.190
I want to get my hands on one and
I want to travel around the world...

19:58.330 --> 20:00.230
That's my dream!

20:01.600 --> 20:04.535
Sounds like a lot of hot
air from a lunkhead...

20:04.870 --> 20:06.201
Lunkhead?

20:06.338 --> 20:08.135
I mean a real idiot!

20:11.443 --> 20:13.343
Ryoma, you can have this.

20:16.281 --> 20:17.305
Izumi...

20:17.750 --> 20:20.241
In return, when you do get
your hands on a Kurofune...

20:20.385 --> 20:22.046
...then I want you to send word to me.

20:22.187 --> 20:24.519
Take me with you around the world!

20:31.797 --> 20:33.458
It's a promise.

20:42.674 --> 20:45.837
Miss Sanako, this is
the kind of man I am.

20:46.178 --> 20:49.079
You should forget about
me, and marry someone else.

20:49.314 --> 20:51.680
Are you saying you don't like me?

20:53.018 --> 20:55.145
I love you, but...

20:59.691 --> 21:03.183
Then, I'll wait until the
day you get your Kurofune...

21:03.762 --> 21:05.059
...I will wait!

21:06.765 --> 21:09.996
From this moment on, Ryoma
Sakamoto became a part of history...

21:10.102 --> 21:12.400
...and turned to his monumental task.

21:12.805 --> 21:15.706
Swept up in the furious tide of change...

21:15.841 --> 21:20.540
<i>To be continued...</i>

21:31.690 --> 21:43.727
<i>Those summer stars, I looked up at</i>
<i>them alone when I was a troubled child.</i>

21:44.002 --> 21:53.741
<i>My loneliness and the vast night</i>
<i>sky, melting and shining in eternity.</i>

21:53.879 --> 22:02.878
<i>I just don't know what this</i>
<i>dream means, if it leads to love...</i>

22:03.021 --> 22:13.693
<i>Even if it's just "hello,"</i>
<i>I want to hear your voice.</i>

22:14.733 --> 22:20.865
<i>The person I am today</i>
<i>is about to disappear...</i>

22:21.240 --> 22:24.232
<i>What is it that will hold me back?</i>

22:25.110 --> 22:31.379
<i>Will it be you? I won't ask you now.</i>

22:31.683 --> 22:37.178
<i>Maybe if we ever meet again...</i>

22:51.937 --> 22:54.371
Soushi Okita, and Toshizo Hijikata...

22:54.640 --> 22:56.870
If I ever catch you laying
a hand on a friend of mine...

22:56.975 --> 22:59.443
...then I'll take that dream of
yours, and smash it to pieces!

23:00.145 --> 23:01.908
Next episode of the Age of Chaos...

23:02.014 --> 23:03.413
<i>Shinsengumi</i>

23:03.515 --> 23:05.847
Pay close attention, and wait!
